","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStem","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Stems can be down, up, none, or double. For down and up stems, the position attributes can be used to specify","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stem length. The relative values specify the end of the stem relative to the program default. Default values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specify an absolute end stem position. Negative values of relative-y that would flip a stem instead of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortening it are ignored. A stem element associated with a rest refers to a stemlet.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStem/color":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc: